WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:01.901
[music playing]

00:00:01.967 --> 00:00:04.103
 Jason, Don, congratulations.

00:00:04.203 --> 00:00:06.840
You've made it into the third
round of this competition.

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.575
We're sending you back
to your home forges

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:11.810
to recreate an iconic
weapon from history.

00:00:11.877 --> 00:00:16.749
That weapon is the scissor.

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.317
 [laughing] Oh god.

00:00:18.384 --> 00:00:19.252
 Oh god.

00:00:19.318 --> 00:00:21.187
 Well, good luck, bladesmiths.

00:00:21.287 --> 00:00:23.123
We'll see you in five days.

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:30.230 line:14%
[music playing]

00:00:31.931 --> 00:00:35.602
 Day one, feels good
to be in my own forge.

00:00:35.668 --> 00:00:36.803
I've never built armor before.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:38.571
I've never shaped
sheet metal before.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:42.175
I need a book, "Armor
for Dummies," you know.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:42.942
They don't make it.

00:00:43.009 --> 00:00:43.777
I looked.

00:00:45.778 --> 00:00:48.548
Two billets I'm making right now
are going to be for the blade.

00:00:48.648 --> 00:00:50.917
I'm going to twist one one
way, and I'm going to twist

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:51.951
the other one the other way.

00:00:52.017 --> 00:00:53.453
I just like the way it looks.

00:00:53.519 --> 00:00:56.855
I almost screwed that up
twisted it the same direction.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:01:00.160
[music playing]

00:01:01.226 --> 00:01:03.663
JASON: I'm going up
against Don from Texas.

00:01:03.763 --> 00:01:05.198
Oklahoma always beats Texas.

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:10.503
DON: I'm not really familiar
with a gladiator scissor.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.672 line:8%
But since it is
armoring, I've been doing

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.406 line:14%
armoring for about 25 years.

00:01:14.506 --> 00:01:17.243
I'm sure I can overcome any
challenges that come up for it.

00:01:17.343 --> 00:01:19.312
I'm using a coarse
wrought iron combined

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:23.483 line:8%
with high carbon steel to
make a composite welded blade.

00:01:23.583 --> 00:01:25.118 line:8%
I have no idea what
that came off of.

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:29.054 line:8%
Just part of my 500
pounds of stuff.

00:01:29.121 --> 00:01:30.456
Hey, man, we're Texas.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:32.458
We're bigger and better,
and our blades are better.

00:01:32.525 --> 00:01:33.459
[laughing]

00:01:33.526 --> 00:01:35.261 line:14%
[music playing]

00:01:35.328 --> 00:01:36.729 line:14%
JASON: Today's armor day.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:38.831 line:8%
It's the big experiment day,
but seems like all week's

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:39.966
been an experiment.

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.333
Yesterday I got a
pattern cut out.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:45.138
I'm going to try to get
the gauntlet shape today.

00:01:45.238 --> 00:01:46.806
I have this big
piece of pipe, so I

00:01:46.872 --> 00:01:48.541
can wrap the metal around it.

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.009
I'm just trying to
beat [bleep] of it

00:01:50.109 --> 00:01:52.011
until it goes
where I want it to.

00:01:52.077 --> 00:01:54.514
I'm probably doing this
the hardest [bleep]

00:01:54.614 --> 00:01:56.182
possible way there is.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:03.723
So I've got it lined
up with my marks.

00:02:03.823 --> 00:02:06.091
Now I'm going to throw a
little tack weld on each end

00:02:06.192 --> 00:02:09.462
and then start getting
the seams closer together.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:12.664 line:8%
And that almost looks
like I meant to do it.

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.033 line:14%
[thunder clap]

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.535 line:14%
[music playing]

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:17.937 line:8%
DON: My whole gauntlet section
is done in three pieces.

00:02:18.004 --> 00:02:19.505
The only thing I
have left to do is

00:02:19.605 --> 00:02:22.875
to make sure all the parts fit
back together, there's no warps

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:24.009
in there that I can't take out.

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:26.445
Problem I had the first time.

00:02:26.545 --> 00:02:29.282
I'm trying to get
the main cone put on.

00:02:29.382 --> 00:02:31.284
It's driving me nuts.

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.286
There's a slight
warp in it that keeps

00:02:34.386 --> 00:02:36.156
catching on the inner layer.

00:02:38.724 --> 00:02:40.426
[sighing] Turn it.

00:02:43.763 --> 00:02:49.636
[grunting] Damn it.

00:02:53.539 --> 00:02:54.207
All right.

00:02:54.274 --> 00:02:55.474
One more time.

00:02:55.574 --> 00:02:59.211
I'm trying to get
the main cone put on.

00:02:59.311 --> 00:03:02.214
There's a slight
warp in it that keeps

00:03:02.314 --> 00:03:03.850
catching on the inner layer.

00:03:10.589 --> 00:03:12.458
There we go.

00:03:12.525 --> 00:03:13.725
Oh.

00:03:13.826 --> 00:03:14.727
That was pain.

00:03:17.229 --> 00:03:19.098 line:14%
 This is billet number three.

00:03:19.198 --> 00:03:21.300
I have a billet of damascus.

00:03:21.366 --> 00:03:23.469
I'm not 100% satisfied with it.

00:03:23.569 --> 00:03:25.905
I don't think it's going to
look the way that I want.

00:03:25.972 --> 00:03:29.141
I'm going to start over with
just uh, some plain steel.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:33.012
I did not want to be
forging on day four.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:34.780
I'm going with a W2.

00:03:34.847 --> 00:03:36.015
It's going to look good.

00:03:36.115 --> 00:03:37.349
It's going to have
to look that I want,

00:03:37.416 --> 00:03:39.818
and I'm not going to be
wasting any more time.

00:03:39.885 --> 00:03:41.654
I'm starting to get the blade
pretty close to the shape

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:45.592
I want, keeping my
measurements in mind.

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:46.659
Let's get it done.

00:03:46.726 --> 00:03:50.730
[music playing]

00:03:56.435 --> 00:03:58.704
Even though I don't like
the way the blade looks,

00:03:58.771 --> 00:04:01.240
performance-wise, though, I
think it's going to perform

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:02.642
just as good as Don's.

00:04:02.708 --> 00:04:04.877
If I lose, I guess
he just got lucky.

00:04:04.977 --> 00:04:07.079
Even a blind squirrel get a
nut every once in a while.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:10.817 line:14%
[laughing]

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.619 line:8%
 All I have left to
do is sharpen the blade

00:04:13.686 --> 00:04:15.488
and then do a little
bit of testing.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.123
Wouldn't don't want to
trip while holding this.

00:04:17.223 --> 00:04:18.458
That would really suck.

00:04:21.027 --> 00:04:22.461
I want to make sure
nothing's going

00:04:22.561 --> 00:04:25.531
to rattle loose when the judges
start hitting stuff with it.

00:04:25.632 --> 00:04:26.198
That would hurt.

00:04:26.265 --> 00:04:27.634
Now the final test.

00:04:31.103 --> 00:04:35.108
It rubs on a knuckle slightly,
but you know, to be honest,

00:04:35.174 --> 00:04:36.609
I didn't even notice
that until afterwards

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:38.811
because I was just having
too much fun swinging

00:04:38.878 --> 00:04:40.780
and cutting things with it.

00:04:40.880 --> 00:04:43.016
DAVID: All right gentlemen,
this is the sharpness test.

00:04:43.082 --> 00:04:44.650
To test the sharpness
of your edge,

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:47.085
I'm going to attack our
sandman here several times,

00:04:47.186 --> 00:04:48.888
see how they do.

00:04:48.988 --> 00:04:50.089
Jason, you're up first.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:51.057
Are you ready for this?
- Yes, sir.

00:04:51.123 --> 00:04:51.857
DAVID: All right.

00:04:51.924 --> 00:04:55.061
[music playing]

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.604
[laughing] All right.

00:05:05.704 --> 00:05:07.272
The handle feels
really good in my hand,

00:05:07.339 --> 00:05:09.809
but the shape of
your blade not being

00:05:09.875 --> 00:05:12.778
as deep a crescent made
it a little bit more

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:14.647
difficult to slash.

00:05:14.747 --> 00:05:17.550
All in all, solid and
it's got a good look.

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:18.116
Nicely done.

00:05:18.183 --> 00:05:18.884
 Thank you.

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:19.685
 All right, Don.

00:05:19.752 --> 00:05:20.586
You ready?

00:05:20.653 --> 00:05:21.119
 I'm ready.

00:05:21.220 --> 00:05:24.590
[music playing]

00:05:39.771 --> 00:05:43.242
 Don, I like the way this is
set up, tighter around the arm.

00:05:43.309 --> 00:05:46.379
But right here at
my hand, my knuckle

00:05:46.445 --> 00:05:48.914
is just pounding into the side.

00:05:49.015 --> 00:05:51.817
You can see it slashed
pretty easily on the arm,

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:55.955
and then on the forward punch,
didn't quite get the slash

00:05:56.055 --> 00:05:57.189
that I was looking for.

00:05:57.255 --> 00:05:59.491
 I'm feeling a little nervous.

00:05:59.591 --> 00:06:01.226
It didn't perform like I wanted.

00:06:01.326 --> 00:06:02.594
I think Jason had the edge here.

00:06:02.661 --> 00:06:04.697
His was a more comfortable
fit across the hand.

00:06:04.764 --> 00:06:06.265
 All in all,
though, did the job.

00:06:06.365 --> 00:06:07.500
 Thank you.

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:08.701
DAVID: Next up, I'll
give you to Doug.

00:06:08.768 --> 00:06:11.137
 Bladesmiths, this
is a kill test.

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.839
To see what kind of lethal
damage your weapon will do,

00:06:13.906 --> 00:06:16.375
I will take your scissor
and I will deliver killing

00:06:16.475 --> 00:06:18.511
blows on this ballistics dummy.

00:06:18.611 --> 00:06:19.612
Jason, you're up first.

00:06:19.679 --> 00:06:20.146
You ready?

00:06:20.213 --> 00:06:21.013
 Let's do it.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:25.051
[music playing]

00:06:30.022 --> 00:06:31.424
[laughing]

00:06:31.491 --> 00:06:34.160
 First up, the minute I put
my hand in, your handle--

00:06:34.260 --> 00:06:39.364
It's not directly in line
with my fist, so slightly off.

00:06:39.465 --> 00:06:41.967
But as you can see, I can
still wield the weapon.

00:06:42.034 --> 00:06:46.304
The laceration was deep
into this cavity right here,

00:06:46.405 --> 00:06:48.440
so you've got a
very sharp blade.

00:06:48.541 --> 00:06:51.376
The hook you have penetrated
right into the heart

00:06:51.443 --> 00:06:52.879
on the back hand draw.

00:06:52.945 --> 00:06:57.516
It lacerates and cuts
everything out and disembowel

00:06:57.583 --> 00:06:59.585
this ballistics dummy.

00:06:59.685 --> 00:07:02.354
Your weapon, sir, will kill.

00:07:02.455 --> 00:07:03.188
Good job, sir.

00:07:03.288 --> 00:07:04.356
 Thank you.

00:07:04.457 --> 00:07:06.258
 Don, your turn.

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.260
 Let's have some fun.

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.827
DOUG: Let's do this.

00:07:08.928 --> 00:07:12.432
[music playing]

00:07:15.802 --> 00:07:19.071
DON: [laughing]

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.339
 Good.

00:07:20.439 --> 00:07:21.807
DOUG: Don, let's talk
about your weapon.

00:07:21.873 --> 00:07:24.009
What I like about your
weapon is that it's

00:07:24.076 --> 00:07:25.678
in line with the handle.

00:07:25.744 --> 00:07:29.215
On the initial cut here, it
lacerated right through there.

00:07:29.315 --> 00:07:31.517
And in this back
hand hook, your edge

00:07:31.584 --> 00:07:35.988
is deep to go in here and
right into that cavity.

00:07:36.088 --> 00:07:37.222
Your weapon will kill.

00:07:37.322 --> 00:07:38.623
 Thank you.

00:07:38.724 --> 00:07:39.992
 All right, gentlemen,
this is the strength test.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:42.527
Now the scissor was used
in gladiatorial combat

00:07:42.594 --> 00:07:44.497
for both attack and defense.

00:07:44.564 --> 00:07:46.932
Now to test the strength and
durability of your weapon,

00:07:47.032 --> 00:07:49.969
we will clamp them into
our mechanical device here.

00:07:50.035 --> 00:07:52.972
The blade's going to come down
and strike the armored cuff

00:07:53.072 --> 00:07:55.441
of your weapon twice, and then
your weapon is going to be

00:07:55.507 --> 00:07:56.976
launched into this breastplate.

00:07:57.042 --> 00:07:58.443
Jason, I've already
got yours strapped in,

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.277
so are you ready to go?

00:07:59.378 --> 00:08:00.112
 Let's do it.

00:08:00.179 --> 00:08:00.980
DAVID: OK.

00:08:10.923 --> 00:08:14.560
[music playing]

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:20.766
 Just the slightest roll.

00:08:20.866 --> 00:08:23.269
It's not deformed
beyond being sharp.

00:08:23.335 --> 00:08:27.139
And then you can see where the
sword came down and hit it,

00:08:27.239 --> 00:08:28.741
caused a bit of deformation.

00:08:28.841 --> 00:08:31.877
And then I think we were pushed
just a little further offline.

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:34.413
It-- Right in here,
it looks like it

00:08:34.513 --> 00:08:37.016
kind of waffled just a bit.

00:08:37.082 --> 00:08:40.219
But everything is still
tight, still sharp.

00:08:40.319 --> 00:08:41.220
Nicely done.

00:08:41.320 --> 00:08:42.121
 Thank you.

00:08:42.221 --> 00:08:43.355
 So Don, you're ready?

00:08:43.455 --> 00:08:44.156
 I'm ready.

00:08:44.223 --> 00:08:47.727
[music playing]

00:08:54.667 --> 00:08:57.536
 So looking at this, I
can I'm having a hard time

00:08:57.602 --> 00:08:59.638
finding where the
sword hit it, and

00:08:59.704 --> 00:09:03.042
there's one teeny little mark.

00:09:03.108 --> 00:09:06.311
Blade's still tight, and that
edge is still a razor blade.

00:09:06.378 --> 00:09:07.946
There's no rolling at all.

00:09:08.047 --> 00:09:09.047
Very well done.

00:09:09.114 --> 00:09:10.115
It's nice.

00:09:10.215 --> 00:09:12.217
 Thank you.

00:09:12.318 --> 00:09:14.452
[music playing]

00:09:14.553 --> 00:09:15.821
 Bladesmiths,
you've worked very

00:09:15.887 --> 00:09:18.524
hard to recreate
weapons that we've never

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:20.493
seen here in the forge before.

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:22.328
However, in this competition,
there can only be

00:09:22.394 --> 00:09:24.396
one "Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:24.463 --> 00:09:31.136
And that champion is Don.

00:09:31.203 --> 00:09:33.939
Congratulations, you are the
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:09:34.006 --> 00:09:35.073
 Yeah.

00:09:35.140 --> 00:09:36.342
Thank you.

00:09:36.442 --> 00:09:38.444
 Jason, unfortunately your
blade did not make the cut.

00:09:38.544 --> 00:09:39.979
David Baker will explain.

00:09:40.079 --> 00:09:42.915
 Jason, what this came down
to was the strength test.

00:09:43.015 --> 00:09:45.751 line:8%
As a gladiator's weapon,
it's got to be strong.

00:09:45.851 --> 00:09:47.619 line:8%
That rolled edge
and the deformation

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:49.755 line:8%
you took from the
hit on the cuff?

00:09:49.855 --> 00:09:52.525
Well that's why we're
sending you home.

00:09:52.591 --> 00:09:55.694
 Jason please surrender
to your scissor.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:57.196
JASON: I spent five
days making something

00:09:57.296 --> 00:09:58.731
I've never made before.

00:09:58.831 --> 00:10:01.366
I went up against a guy who
builds armor quite often.

00:10:01.433 --> 00:10:02.568
I held my own against him.

00:10:02.634 --> 00:10:04.503
I'm pretty proud of that fact.

00:10:04.603 --> 00:10:07.873
I loved every minute
of this experience.

00:10:07.940 --> 00:10:10.609
 Don, congratulations, you are
the "Forged in Fire" champion

00:10:10.676 --> 00:10:13.645
and will be receiving
that check for 10 grand.

00:10:13.712 --> 00:10:14.579
How do you feel right now?

00:10:14.646 --> 00:10:16.081
 Man, I feel fantastic.

00:10:16.148 --> 00:10:18.884
It feels great to be a
"Forged in Fire" champion.

00:10:18.984 --> 00:10:20.085
$10,000.

00:10:20.185 --> 00:10:21.887
I'd like to get something
nice for my wife.

00:10:21.953 --> 00:10:23.322
We kind of had a
little fun, you know,

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:25.757
making jokes at each other
about Texas versus Oklahoma.

00:10:25.824 --> 00:10:28.159
Yeah, I'm glad to see
Texas came out on top.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:30.730
[laughing] Woo!

